*** UPI ***

Our upi id is like a IP address , where each upi belongs to bank account --> this is maintained by NPCI

PIN/Biometrics etc is used for authentication/authorization


Sender ---> My Bank --> it gets authenticated etc at source bank ---> NPCI ---> Receiver bank 

Banks can also cache some of inputs (like you transferring to your top 20 friends) , NPCI comes into place only when banks don't have cache.


